{"base_rate":0.38451443569553806,"brier":0.12232440944881891,"bss":0.4831284746428752,"bss_hi":0.5642075449863215,"bss_lo":0.40188534079923743,"chart":{"base":[560.6,105.4],"fp":[278.1,322.4],"lead":"62,250.8 272,227.1 482,173.9 692,113.8","note":{"base":"skill 0.48 — higher than 86% of cities","fp":"low end +8pp, high end +7pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.1 °C — better than 57% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 5%; promised 99% → rained 92%"},"rel":"62,444.4 156.2,358 490.4,189.3 683.6,67.9"},"country":"DE","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.07175853018372702,"ess":378.3889695518304,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Frankfurt am Main</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Frankfurt am Main rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 5 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>92%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>5%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 762 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nFRANKFURT/MAIN-WESTEND, 1.7 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.48, ranked 19 of\n134 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(7&ndash;40) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>5%</b></td><td class='num'>300</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>5%</td><td class='num'><b>15%</b></td><td class='num'>78</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>24%</td><td class='num'><b>35%</b></td><td class='num'>78</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>55%</td><td class='num'><b>61%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>81%</td><td class='num'><b>68%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>92%</b></td><td class='num'>153</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">5 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Frankfurt am Main</b> <span class=\"muted\">DE</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">5 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.48</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>7&ndash;40\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 134</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>762 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Frankfurt am Main &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Frankfurt am Main\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text clas